<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Notation and Definitions</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The symbol <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> represents
the set of real numbers, <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}_{+}=\left\{\ell\in\mathbb{R}:\ell\geq 0\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}_{+}=\left\{\ell\in\mathbb{R}:\ell\geq 0\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the vector space of <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-tuple
of real numbers.
The transpose of a matrix <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is denoted by <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> stand for the identity matrix. The symbol <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rVert\cdot\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0.055em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rVert\cdot\rVert</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the Euclidean norm on <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a Lebesgue measurable function <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\colon\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\colon\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>,
define the norm <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rVert u\rVert_{(t_{1},t_{2})}=\text{ess}\sup_{t\in(t_{1},t_{2})}\rVert u(t)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>ess</mtext><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rVert u\rVert_{(t_{1},t_{2})}=\text{ess}\sup_{t\in(t_{1},t_{2})}\rVert u(t)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math>
for <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t_{1},t_{2})\subseteq\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t_{1},t_{2})\subseteq\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\infty}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\infty}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>
the space of functions <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rVert u\rVert_{\infty}:=\rVert u\rVert_{(-\infty,+\infty)}&lt;+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">&lt;</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rVert u\rVert_{\infty}:=\rVert u\rVert_{(-\infty,+\infty)}&lt;+\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">A continuous function <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:\mathbb{R}_{+}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:\mathbb{R}_{+}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs
to class <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{K}</annotation></semantics></math> if it is strictly increasing and <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{K}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{K}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> means that <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is also unbounded.
A continuous function <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta:\mathbb{R}_{+}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta:\mathbb{R}_{+}\times\mathbb{R}_{+}\to\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>
belongs to class <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(\cdot,r)\in\mathscr{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(\cdot,r)\in\mathscr{K}</annotation></semantics></math>
and <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(r,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(r,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is a decreasing to zero function for any fixed
<math id="A1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For this system (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), we have the following assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmasmp1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_asmp">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmasmp1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmasmp1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We assume that the system (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) is forward complete, i.e., for all <math id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{L}_{\infty}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{L}_{\infty}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, the solution <math id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t,x_{0},u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t,x_{0},u)</annotation></semantics></math> is uniquely defined for all <math id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A1.Thmasmp1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The formal definitions of ISS and convergence are provided below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmmydef1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_mydef">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmmydef1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmmydef1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A forward complete system (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) is
input-to-state stable (ISS) if there exist <math id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\in\mathscr{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\in\mathscr{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\mathscr{KL}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\mathscr{KL}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x(t,x_{0},u)\|\leq\beta(\|x_{0}\|,t)+\gamma(\|u\|_{\infty}),\quad\forall t\in\mathbb{R}_{+}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x(t,x_{0},u)\|\leq\beta(\|x_{0}\|,t)+\gamma(\|u\|_{\infty}),\quad\forall t\in\mathbb{R}_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any <math id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{L}_{\infty}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{L}_{\infty}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The model (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>) is convergent if it admits a unique bounded solution for <math id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that is globally asymptotically stable (GAS).
<span id="A1.Thmmydef1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theorem Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 The Training-Inference Gap in FM ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmrefproofx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_refproof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Proof</span>.</h6>
<div id="Thmrefproofx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">To be clear and concise, we define and rearrange some notations.
For an initial value <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t_{n}):=\psi_{t}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t_{n}):=\psi_{t}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{n}:=\phi_{n}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{n}:=\phi_{n}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> represent the ground truth and the model output, respectively. Then we can derive that</p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x(t_{n+1})-x_{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x(t_{n+1})-x_{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="4" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=x(t_{n})+\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{\tau}(x(\tau))\,d\tau-x_{n}-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=x(t_{n})+\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{\tau}(x(\tau))\,d\tau-x_{n}-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E1Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{n-1}+\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{\tau}(x(\tau))-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})\,d\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{n-1}+\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{\tau}(x(\tau))-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})\,d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E1Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{n-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\varepsilon_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E1Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}f(\tau,x(\tau))-u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))+u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))-u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})+u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})\,d\tau." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}f(\tau,x(\tau))-u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))+u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))-u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})+u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})\,d\tau.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We will split the integral in expression (<a href="#A2.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) into three parts and estimate them separately. The first part</p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{\tau}(x(\tau))-u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))\,d\tau|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{\tau}(x(\tau))-u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))\,d\tau|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}x^{\prime}(\tau)-x^{\prime}(t_{n})\,d\tau|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}x^{\prime}(\tau)-x^{\prime}(t_{n})\,d\tau|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E2Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}x^{\prime\prime}(t_{n}+\theta(\tau-t_{n}))(\tau-t_{n})\,d\tau|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}x^{\prime\prime}(t_{n}+\theta(\tau-t_{n}))(\tau-t_{n})\,d\tau|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E2Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|x^{\prime\prime}(t_{n}+\theta(\tau-t_{n}))\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}(\tau-t_{n})\,d\tau|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|x^{\prime\prime}(t_{n}+\theta(\tau-t_{n}))\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}(\tau-t_{n})\,d\tau|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E2Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\frac{1}{2}\tau_{n}^{2}x^{\prime\prime}(t_{n}+\theta(\bar{t}-t_{n}))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\frac{1}{2}\tau_{n}^{2}x^{\prime\prime}(t_{n}+\theta(\bar{t}-t_{n}))|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E2Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E2Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{n}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{n}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\theta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\theta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{t}\in(t_{n},t_{n+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{t}\in(t_{n},t_{n+1})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\max_{0\leq t\leq 1}|x^{\prime\prime}(t)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\max_{0\leq t\leq 1}|x^{\prime\prime}(t)|</annotation></semantics></math>. The second and third equalities in (<a href="#A2.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>) use the Differentiation Mean Value Theorem (MVT) and Integration MVT, respectively.
Using the Lipschitz condition, the second part in (<a href="#A2.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) derives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))-u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})|=\tau_{n}\,|(u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))-u_{t_{n}}(x_{n}))|\leq L_{u}\tau_{n}|x(t_{n})-x_{n}|=L_{u}\tau_{n}\varepsilon_{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))-u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})|=\tau_{n}\,|(u_{t_{n}}(x(t_{n}))-u_{t_{n}}(x_{n}))|\leq L_{u}\tau_{n}|x(t_{n})-x_{n}|=L_{u}\tau_{n}\varepsilon_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">The third part <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})d\tau|\leq\delta\tau_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\int_{t_{n}}^{t_{n+1}}u_{t_{n}}(x_{n})-v_{t_{n}}(x_{n})d\tau|\leq\delta\tau_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Plugging these into (<a href="#A2.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>) and taking the absolute values yield</p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varepsilon_{n+1}|\leq(1+L_{u}\tau_{n})|\varepsilon_{n}|+\delta\tau_{n}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{n}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varepsilon_{n+1}|\leq(1+L_{u}\tau_{n})|\varepsilon_{n}|+\delta\tau_{n}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{n}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">or equivalently,</p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varepsilon_{n+1}|-|\varepsilon_{n}|\leq L_{u}\tau_{n}|\varepsilon_{n}|+\delta\tau_{n}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{n}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varepsilon_{n+1}|-|\varepsilon_{n}|\leq L_{u}\tau_{n}|\varepsilon_{n}|+\delta\tau_{n}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{n}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Summing <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>) from <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varepsilon_{m}|\leq L_{u}\Sigma_{j=0}^{m-1}\tau_{j}|\varepsilon_{j}|+\Sigma_{j=0}^{m-1}(\delta\tau_{j}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{j}^{2})+|\varepsilon_{0}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varepsilon_{m}|\leq L_{u}\Sigma_{j=0}^{m-1}\tau_{j}|\varepsilon_{j}|+\Sigma_{j=0}^{m-1}(\delta\tau_{j}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{j}^{2})+|\varepsilon_{0}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Appling Grönwall inequality (Lemma <a href="#Thmlem1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) we get</p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\varepsilon_{m}|\leq\exp{(L_{u}t_{m-1})}\left(\Sigma_{j=0}^{m-1}(\delta\tau_{j}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{j}^{2})+|\varepsilon_{0}|\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\varepsilon_{m}|\leq\exp{(L_{u}t_{m-1})}\left(\Sigma_{j=0}^{m-1}(\delta\tau_{j}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{j}^{2})+|\varepsilon_{0}|\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">By taking <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=N</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the final result in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 The Training-Inference Gap in FM ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).
It is noted that Lemma 1 employs specialized scaling techniques designed for variable step-size schemes.
On a uniform grid, i.e., <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall\,i\in[0,N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\,i\in[0,N]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{i}=\tau_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{i}=\tau_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can have a shaper error estimate. It follows directly from (<a href="#A2.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>) that</p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex4X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\varepsilon_{n+1}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\varepsilon_{n+1}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})|\varepsilon_{n}|+R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})|\varepsilon_{n}|+R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{2}|\varepsilon_{n-1}|+(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})R+R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{2}|\varepsilon_{n-1}|+(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})R+R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\cdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex4Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex4Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n+1}|\varepsilon_{0}|+\left[(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}+(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n-1}+\cdots+1\right]R\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n+1}|\varepsilon_{0}|+\left[(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}+(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n-1}+\cdots+1\right]R\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.12" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:=\delta\tau_{0}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:=\delta\tau_{0}+\frac{1}{2}M\tau_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex5X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\varepsilon_{n}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\varepsilon_{n}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}|\varepsilon_{0}|+\left[\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{j}\right]R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}|\varepsilon_{0}|+\left[\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{j}\right]R</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex5Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex5Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}|\varepsilon_{0}|+\frac{R}{\tau_{0}L_{u}}\left[(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}-1\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}|\varepsilon_{0}|+\frac{R}{\tau_{0}L_{u}}\left[(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}-1\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Considering <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp{(n\tau_{0}L_{u})}&gt;(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp{(n\tau_{0}L_{u})}&gt;(1+\tau_{0}L_{u})^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain</p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E5X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E5X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{n}\leq\exp({L_{u}\tau_{0}n})\varepsilon_{0}+\frac{M\tau_{0}+2\delta}{2L}(\exp{(L_{u}\tau_{0}n})-1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{n}\leq\exp({L_{u}\tau_{0}n})\varepsilon_{0}+\frac{M\tau_{0}+2\delta}{2L}(\exp{(L_{u}\tau_{0}n})-1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.14" class="ltx_p">Taking <math id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=N</annotation></semantics></math> yields the final estimate (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 The Training-Inference Gap in FM ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). <span id="Thmrefproofx1.p1.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the sake of completeness, in the following we put the standard discrete Grönwall inequality, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liao &amp; Zhang (2021, Lemma 3.1)</a></cite>, and its proof.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmlem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the time sequences <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\xi_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\xi_{k}\}_{k=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{V_{k}\}_{k=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{V_{k}\}_{k=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be nonnegative. If</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{n}\leq\lambda\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}\tau_{j}V_{j}+\sum_{j=0}^{n}\xi_{j}\quad\text{for }1\leq n\leq N," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{n}\leq\lambda\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}\tau_{j}V_{j}+\sum_{j=0}^{n}\xi_{j}\quad\text{for }1\leq n\leq N,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{n}\leq\exp(\lambda t_{n-1})\sum_{j=0}^{n}\xi_{j}\quad\text{for }1\leq n\leq N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{n}\leq\exp(\lambda t_{n-1})\sum_{j=0}^{n}\xi_{j}\quad\text{for }1\leq n\leq N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmreproofx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_reproof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Proof</span> (<span id="Thmreproofx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof.</span> ).</h6>
<div id="Thmreproofx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmreproofx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under the induction hypothesis <math id="Thmreproofx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{j}\leq\exp(\lambda t_{j-1})\sum_{k=0}^{j}\xi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{j}\leq\exp(\lambda t_{j-1})\sum_{k=0}^{j}\xi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmreproofx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, the desired inequality for the index <math id="Thmreproofx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> follows directly from</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}\tau_{j}\exp(\lambda t_{j-1})\leq\lambda\int_{0}^{t_{n-1}}\exp(\lambda t)\,dt=\exp(\lambda t_{n-1})-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}\tau_{j}\exp(\lambda t_{j-1})\leq\lambda\int_{0}^{t_{n-1}}\exp(\lambda t)\,dt=\exp(\lambda t_{n-1})-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmreproofx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The principle of induction completes the proof.
<span id="Thmreproofx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 MLE Fine-tuning ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h3>

<div id="Thmreproofx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_reproof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Proof</span>.</h6>
<div id="Thmreproofx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmreproofx2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Under the Assumption <a href="#Thmasmp1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 3.2 MLE Fine-tuning ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> , we have</p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E6X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x|x_{0},x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x|x_{0},x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E6X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\frac{\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-x_{1})^{T}\Sigma^{-1}(x-x_{1})\right)}{\sqrt{(2\pi)^{d}|\Sigma|}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\frac{\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}(x-x_{1})^{T}\Sigma^{-1}(x-x_{1})\right)}{\sqrt{(2\pi)^{d}|\Sigma|}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmreproofx2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">When <math id="Thmreproofx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\mathrm{diag}(\sigma^{1},\cdots,\sigma^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\mathrm{diag}(\sigma^{1},\cdots,\sigma^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix with all positive entries, it follows from <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Theorem Proofs ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> that</p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E7X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x|x_{0},x_{1})=-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{(x^{i}-x_{1}^{i})^{2}}{\sigma^{i}}-\log\sqrt{(2\pi)^{d}\prod_{i=1}^{d}\sigma^{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p_{1}(x|x_{0},x_{1})=-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{(x^{i}-x_{1}^{i})^{2}}{\sigma^{i}}-\log\sqrt{(2\pi)^{d}\prod_{i=1}^{d}\sigma^{d}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmreproofx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmreproofx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the second term is independent of <math id="Thmreproofx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, considering the relation <math id="Thmreproofx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1}(x_{0}|x_{1})=x_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1}(x_{0}|x_{1})=x_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmreproofx2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{N}(x_{0}|x_{1})=\psi_{1}(x_{0}|x_{1})-\hat{\phi}_{N}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{N}(x_{0}|x_{1})=\psi_{1}(x_{0}|x_{1})-\hat{\phi}_{N}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>,
maximizing
<math id="Thmreproofx2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{0},x_{1})}\left[\log p_{1}\left(\hat{\phi}_{N}(x_{0})|x_{1}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>N</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{0},x_{1})}\left[\log p_{1}\left(\hat{\phi}_{N}(x_{0})|x_{1}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math>
is equivalent to minimizing
<math id="Thmreproofx2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{0},x_{1})}\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}(\varepsilon_{N}^{i}(x_{0}|x_{1}))^{2}/\sigma^{i}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q(x_{0},x_{1})}\left[\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{d}(\varepsilon_{N}^{i}(x_{0}|x_{1}))^{2}/\sigma^{i}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmreproofx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmreproofx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In the case where <math id="Thmreproofx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is a scalar matrix, i.e., <math id="Thmreproofx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma=\sigma I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma=\sigma I</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmreproofx2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, following the same procedure and discarding the irrelevant coefficient leads to the loss function (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 MLE Fine-tuning ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).
<span id="Thmreproofx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar proofs can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al. (2024)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mei et al. (2022)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Efimov &amp; Aleksandrov (2021)</a></cite>. Here, we briefly outline the general process.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmreproofx3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_reproof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Proof</span> (Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm3" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="Thmreproofx3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmreproofx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a Lyapunov function</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(x)=x^{\top}Px+2\sum_{j=1}^{M}\sum_{i=1}^{k_{j}}\Lambda^{j}_{i}\int_{0}^{W_{j}^{i}x}f_{j}^{i}(s)ds," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(x)=x^{\top}Px+2\sum_{j=1}^{M}\sum_{i=1}^{k_{j}}\Lambda^{j}_{i}\int_{0}^{W_{j}^{i}x}f_{j}^{i}(s)ds,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmreproofx3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the vector <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{j}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{j}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th row of the matrix <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. It is positive definite and radially unbounded due to Finsler’s Lemma under the condition equation <a href="#S3.E8" title="In Theorem 3. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and Assumption <a href="#Thmasmp2" title="Assumption 2. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Then, taking the derivative of <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, one has</p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{V}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}x\\
f_{1}(W_{1}x)\\
\vdots\\
f_{M}(W_{M}x)\\
g(u)\end{bmatrix}^{\top}Q\begin{bmatrix}x\\
f_{1}(W_{1}x)\\
\vdots\\
f_{M}(W_{M}x)\\
g(u)\end{bmatrix}-x^{\top}\Xi^{0}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{bmatrix}x\\
f_{1}(W_{1}x)\\
\vdots\\
f_{M}(W_{M}x)\\
g(u)\end{bmatrix}^{\top}Q\begin{bmatrix}x\\
f_{1}(W_{1}x)\\
\vdots\\
f_{M}(W_{M}x)\\
g(u)\end{bmatrix}-x^{\top}\Xi^{0}x</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{j=1}^{M}f_{j}(W_{j}x)^{\top}\Xi^{j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)-2\sum_{j=1}^{M}x^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}\Upsilon_{0,j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{j=1}^{M}f_{j}(W_{j}x)^{\top}\Xi^{j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)-2\sum_{j=1}^{M}x^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}\Upsilon_{0,j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-2\sum_{s=1}^{M-1}\sum_{r=s+1}^{M}f_{s}(W_{s}x)^{\top}{W_{s}^{\top}}W_{s}\Upsilon_{s,r}W_{r}^{\top}{W_{r}}f_{r}(W_{r}x)+g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\sum_{s=1}^{M-1}\sum_{r=s+1}^{M}f_{s}(W_{s}x)^{\top}{W_{s}^{\top}}W_{s}\Upsilon_{s,r}W_{r}^{\top}{W_{r}}f_{r}(W_{r}x)+g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-x^{\top}\Xi^{0}x-\sum_{j=1}^{M}f_{j}(W_{j}x)^{\top}\Xi^{j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)-2\sum_{j=1}^{M}x^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}\Upsilon_{0,j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-x^{\top}\Xi^{0}x-\sum_{j=1}^{M}f_{j}(W_{j}x)^{\top}\Xi^{j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)-2\sum_{j=1}^{M}x^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}\Upsilon_{0,j}f_{j}(W_{j}x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-2\sum_{s=1}^{M-1}\sum_{r=s+1}^{M}f_{s}(W_{s}x)^{\top}{W_{s}^{\top}}W_{s}\Upsilon_{s,r}W_{r}^{\top}{W_{r}}f_{r}(W_{r}x)+g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Υ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-2\sum_{s=1}^{M-1}\sum_{r=s+1}^{M}f_{s}(W_{s}x)^{\top}{W_{s}^{\top}}W_{s}\Upsilon_{s,r}W_{r}^{\top}{W_{r}}f_{r}(W_{r}x)+g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr class="ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\alpha(V)+g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\alpha(V)+g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmreproofx3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for a function <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathscr{K}_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒦</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathscr{K}_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sontag &amp; Wang, 1995</a>, Theorem 1)</cite>,
we can verify the first condition of the ISS property due to the form of <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, and the second relation can be recovered via <math id="Thmreproofx3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\geq\alpha^{-1}\left(2g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)\right)\Rightarrow\dot{V}\leq-\frac{1}{2}\alpha(V)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\geq\alpha^{-1}\left(2g(u)^{\top}\Phi g(u)\right)\Rightarrow\dot{V}\leq-\frac{1}{2}\alpha(V)</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that the ISS property of the NN equation <a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> is guaranteed, and so is the boundedness of its solution.
<span id="Thmreproofx3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze the contraction property of (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), we need the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we have
<math id="Thmlem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}(x,\xi)^{\top}p_{j}(x,\xi)\leq\xi^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}L^{j}p_{j}(x,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}(x,\xi)^{\top}p_{j}(x,\xi)\leq\xi^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}L^{j}p_{j}(x,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>
and
<math id="Thmlem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{j}(W_{j}\xi)^{\top}f_{j}(W_{j}\xi)\leq\xi^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}L^{j}f_{j}(W_{j}\xi)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{j}(W_{j}\xi)^{\top}f_{j}(W_{j}\xi)\leq\xi^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}L^{j}f_{j}(W_{j}\xi).</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="Thmlem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmreproofx4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_reproof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Proof</span>.</h6>
<div id="Thmreproofx4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmreproofx4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proof.
It follows from the Lipschitz continuity Assumption <a href="#Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> that <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)|=|f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i}+(W_{j}\xi)^{i})-f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i})|\leq L_{j}^{i}|(W_{j}\xi)^{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)|=|f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i}+(W_{j}\xi)^{i})-f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i})|\leq L_{j}^{i}|(W_{j}\xi)^{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, the superscript <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of the vector.
When <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{j}x)^{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{j}x)^{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)=f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i}+(W_{j}\xi)^{i})-f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)=f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i}+(W_{j}\xi)^{i})-f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> due to the Monotonicity in Assumption <a href="#Thmasmp3" title="Assumption 3. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Then
<math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)\leq L_{j}^{i}(W_{j}\xi)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)\leq L_{j}^{i}(W_{j}\xi)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Multiplying both sides by a non-negative number <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get
<math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)^{2}\leq L_{j}^{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)(W_{j}x)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)^{2}\leq L_{j}^{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)(W_{j}x)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{j}x)^{i}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{j}x)^{i}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)=f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i}+(W_{j}\xi)^{i})-f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i})\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)=f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i}+(W_{j}\xi)^{i})-f_{j}^{i}((W_{j}x)^{i})\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> due to the same Monotonicity Assumption, leading to
<math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)\leq-L_{j}^{i}(W_{j}\xi)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)\leq-L_{j}^{i}(W_{j}\xi)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Multiplying both sides by a non-negative number <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, we get the same result <math id="Thmreproofx4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)^{2}\leq L_{j}^{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)(W_{j}x)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)^{2}\leq L_{j}^{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)(W_{j}x)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmreproofx4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmreproofx4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Summing over <math id="Thmreproofx4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> on both sides gives <math id="Thmreproofx4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)^{2}\leq\sum_{i}L_{j}^{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)(W_{j}x)^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)^{2}\leq\sum_{i}L_{j}^{i}p_{j}^{i}(x,\xi)(W_{j}x)^{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Or equivalently, in a compact from, <math id="Thmreproofx4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}(x,\xi)^{\top}p_{j}(x,\xi)\leq(W_{j}x)^{\top}L_{j}p_{j}(x,\xi)=x^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}L_{j}p_{j}(x,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}(x,\xi)^{\top}p_{j}(x,\xi)\leq(W_{j}x)^{\top}L_{j}p_{j}(x,\xi)=x^{\top}W_{j}^{\top}L_{j}p_{j}(x,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof of the first part of the lemma.
By noting the relation of <math id="Thmreproofx4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(W_{j}x)=f(W_{j}x-0)=p_{j}(0,\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(W_{j}x)=f(W_{j}x-0)=p_{j}(0,\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>, the second part of the lemma holds naturally.
<span id="Thmreproofx4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_floatright"></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmrefproofx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_refproof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem">Proof</span> (Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmthm4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 3.3 Residual MLE Fine-tuning with contraction analysis ‣ 3 On the Fine-Tuning of FM: Motivations and Methods ‣ Fine-Tuning Flow Matching via Maximum Likelihood Estimation of Reconstructions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="Thmrefproofx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmrefproofx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider an positive definite function</p>
<table id="A2.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}(\xi)=\xi^{\top}\tilde{P}\xi+2\sum_{j=1}^{M}\sum_{i=1}^{k_{j}}\tilde{\Lambda}^{j}_{i}\int_{0}^{W_{j}^{i}\xi}f_{j}^{i}(s)ds." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}(\xi)=\xi^{\top}\tilde{P}\xi+2\sum_{j=1}^{M}\sum_{i=1}^{k_{j}}\tilde{\Lambda}^{j}_{i}\int_{0}^{W_{j}^{i}\xi}f_{j}^{i}(s)ds.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmrefproofx2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Taking the time derivative of <math id="Thmrefproofx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dot{\tilde{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>˙</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dot{\tilde{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.EGx4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\begin{array}[]{c}\xi\\
p_{1}(x,\xi)\\
\vdots\\
p_{M}(x,\xi)\\
f_{1}(W_{1}\xi)\\
\vdots\\
f_{M}(W_{M}\xi)\end{array}\right]^{\top}\tilde{Q}\left[\begin{array}[]{c}\xi\\
p_{1}(x,\xi)\\
\vdots\\
p_{M}(x,\xi)\\
f_{1}(W_{1}\xi)\\
\vdots\\
f_{M}(W_{M}\xi)\end{array}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>ξ</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>ξ</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="fal